{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 6, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.2-3b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III was Count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1192. He was the last of the Calabrian dynasty to rule Tripoli. Raymond III was born in 1115 in Calabria. \n\n* **Early Life and Reign** \nRaymond III succeeded his brother Ponthus as Count of Tripoli in 1152. In 1157 he married Eschiva of Alpilles. Raymond III expanded the county by capturing the city of Sidon from the Fatimid Caliphate in 1158. However he lost it in 1166 to the Crusaders. Raymond III also clashed with the Kingdom of Jerusalem over the county's borders. \n\n* **Military Campaigns and foreign relations** \nRaymond III participated in the Third Crusade in 1190 and 1191. He was a guest at the court of King Richard the Lionheart in 1191. Raymond III also clashed with the Kingdom of Sicily in 1192. \n\n* **Death and Legacy** \nRaymond III died in 1192 while on his way back to Tripoli from the Third Crusade. He was succeeded by his brother Bohemond III. The Calabrian dynasty came to an end with Raymond III's death. The County of Tripoli was eventually split between Bohemond III and the Kingdom of Jerusalem.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.0011805477552115917}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.00011586471373448148}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.986915946006775}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -2.2132647037506104}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -6.9141146923357155e-06}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0019252828788012266}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -0.00011705666838679463}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.06802918016910553}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.02141939103603363}, {"token": "115", "logprob": -0.6388193964958191}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -0.00206864345818758}, {"token": " until", "logprob": -0.11444522440433502}, {"token": " his", "logprob": -0.003565385239198804}, {"token": " death", "logprob": -0.00